---
/**
 * The "this page is a draft" notice, as a `cs-callout`.
 *
 * Shown by Starlight on any page with `draft: true` when it is served in dev — a real warning worth keeping,
 * since this site has 16 draft pages carrying unported markup. Starlight's version reaches it through
 * `ContentNotice.astro`, which pulls in its own scoped stylesheet and its `Icon` component; rendering the same
 * thing as a callout drops both and matches every other notice on the site.
 *
 * `FallbackContentNotice` is the other route to `ContentNotice` and is pointed at Empty.astro: it announces
 * untranslated content, and this site has a single locale.
 */
---

<cs-callout variant="warning" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <cs-icon slot="icon" name="warning" variant="fill"/>
  {Astro.locals.t('page.draft')}
</cs-callout>
